},{"id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-p3","title":"Part 3","part_number":3,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3131589-official_cambridge_guide_to_ielts_academic_listening_test_8_3.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-g3-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 21-27","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>What helped Stewart with each of the following stages in making his training film for museum employees?</p><p>Choose SEVEN answers from the box and write the correct letter, A–I, next to Questions 21–27.</p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"matching-dnd-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>finding a location</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">21</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q21\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>deciding on equipment</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">22</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q22\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>writing the script</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">23</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>casting</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">24</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>filming</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">25</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>editing</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">26</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q26\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>designing the DVD cover</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">27</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div></div><div class=\"options-dnd-panel dnd-panel dnd-panel--matching\"><div class=\"dnd-panel-instruction\">Drag and drop an option to fill in each blank.</div><div class=\"dnd-cards-container\"><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"A\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">A.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">advice from friends</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"B\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">B.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">information on a website</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"C\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">C.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">being allowed extra time</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"D\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">D.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">meeting a professional film maker</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"E\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">E.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">good weather conditions</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"F\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">F.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">getting a better computer</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"G\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">G.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">support of a manager</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"H\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">H.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">help from a family member</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"I\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">I.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">work on a previous assignment</span></div></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":7},{"id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-g3-1","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 28-30","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.</p><p><b>Stewart's work placement: benefits to the Central Museum Association</b></p><ul><li>his understanding of the Association's <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">28</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li>the reduction in expense</li><li>increased co-operation between <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li>continuous <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> which led to a better product</li><li>ideas for distribution of the film</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":3}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/official_cambridge_guide_to_ielts_academic_listening_test_8_3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3131590-official_cambridge_guide_to_ielts_academic_listening_test_8_4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"diagram_labelling","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.</p><p><b>New Caledonian crows and the use of tools</b></p><p><b>Examples of animals using tools</b></p><ul><li>some chimpanzees use stones to break nuts</li><li>Betty (New Caledonian crow) made a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> out of wire to move a bucket of food</li><li>Barney (New Caledonian crow) used sticks to find food</li></ul><p><b>New Zealand and Oxford experiment</b></p><ul><li>three stages: crows needed to move a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> in order to reach a short stick; then use the short stick to reach a long stick; then use the long stick to reach food</li></ul><p><b>Oxford research</b></p><ul><li>crows used sticks to investigate whether there was any <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> from an object</li><li>research was inspired by seeing crows using tools on a piece of cloth to investigate a spider design</li><li>Barney used a stick to investigate a snake made of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li>Pierre used a stick to investigate a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li>Corbeau used a stick to investigate a metal toad</li><li>the crows only used sticks for the first contact</li></ul><p><b>Conclusions of above research</b></p><ul><li>ability to plan provides interesting evidence of the birds' cognition</li><li>unclear whether this is evidence of the birds' <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li></ul><p><b>Exeter and Oxford research in New Caledonia</b></p><ul><li>scientists have attached very small cameras to birds' <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li>food in the form of beetle larvae provides plenty of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> for the birds</li><li>larvae's specific <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> composition can be identified in birds that feed on them</li><li>scientists will analyse what the birds include in their <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-official-guide-t8-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/official_cambridge_guide_to_ielts_academic_listening_test_8_4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-q1","part_id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-p1","group_id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"simple documents/documents","correct_answer_variants":["simple documents","documents"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3130162_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-q2","part_id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-p1","group_id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"keyboard","correct_answer_variants":["keyboard"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3130162_2","order_index":2,"points":1},{"id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-q3","part_id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-p1","group_id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"flowers","correct_answer_variants":["flowers"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[3],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3130162_3","order_index":3,"points":1},{"id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-q4","part_id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-p1","group_id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"tools","correct_answer_variants":["tools"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[4],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3130162_4","order_index":4,"points":1},{"id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-q5","part_id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-p1","group_id":"en-official-guide-t8-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"Saturd